Dear Robert,

Please find the Q4 2021 inspection status for the ATU-100. All activities are being tracked against the current RBI intervals defined in QSCP-IP-ATU100 Rev 3, which specifies 3 years for Class 1 sour gas, regenerator overhead and rich amine, and 6 years for the remaining lines.

The current thickness monitoring program continues to utilize the 150 CMLs established during the re-baseline survey documented in LNDE-RPT-20191001-027-R0. We are ensuring all readings are evaluated against t-min to determine remaining life and next inspection dates per site rules.

Regards,  Jennifer Walsh

